# Multi-tournament concurrency

Chess-N-Mates runs **many tournaments at the same time**. Automation (Chess.com auto-compute, standings, fixtures, player dashboard) exists so admins and players are not stuck in a single-event workflow.

## Rules

- Never assume there is only one `active` or “ongoing” competition.
- Prefer lists / filters over `.find(status === "active")` for UI and logic.
- Featured tournaments (`is_featured`) may also be **multiple** — hero/carousels should support several, not one slot.
- Player surfaces (dashboard bars, tournament page, matches) should work when a user is registered in **several** concurrent events.
- Backend jobs (e.g. daily compute) must iterate **all** eligible active competitions.

## Anti-patterns

- Labels like “the ongoing tournament” tied to a single record
- Global `getCurrentCompetition()` style helpers that return one row
- Hiding other live tournaments behind a single featured pick
